     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Thanks! <br><span><br>On Friday, June 30, 2017 at 1:39:02 AM UTC+9:30, Hadley Wickham wrote:</span><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><div dir=\"ltr\">You need to define the grouping yourself:<div><br></div><div><div>library(ggplot2)</div><div><br></div><div>mydf &lt;- data.frame(</div><div>  id = rep(1:90, each = 3),</div><div>  tmt = rep(c(&quot;A&quot;, &quot;B&quot;, &quot;C&quot;), each = 90),</div><div>  time = rep(c(10, 20, 40),90),</div><div>  y = rnorm(270)</div><div>)</div><div><br></div><div>ggplot(mydf, aes(time, y, fill = tmt, group = interaction(time, tmt))) + </div><div>  geom_boxplot()</div></div><div><br></div><div>Hadley</div></div></span><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><span>On Wed, Jun 28, 2017 at 9:57 PM, Emma Knight <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">emmak...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></span><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p>Hi there,<br><br>I am trying to produce a grouped boxplot with unequal spacing along the x axis. <br><br>Here is an example data set and the boxplots I have come up with so far. <br><br>###<br>mydf&lt;-data.frame(id=rep(1:90,each=3),tmt=rep(c(&quot;A&quot;,&quot;B&quot;,&quot;C&quot;),each=90),time=rep(c(10,20,40),90),y=rnorm(270))<br>mydf$time.f&lt;-factor(mydf$time)<br><br>ggplot(data=mydf,aes(x=time.f,y=y,fill=tmt)) + <br>  geom_boxplot()<br><br>ggplot(data=mydf,aes(x=time,y=y,colour=tmt,group=time)) + <br>  geom_boxplot() +<br>  scale_x_continuous(breaks=mydf$time,labels=mydf$time)<br>###<br><br>The first plot results in a grouped boxplot with equal spacing on the x axis.<br> <br><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-TjWTyYUesQs/WVRrSBYHI1I/AAAAAAAAACI/EXh9smfCdF4riP9vi2pbVGqcIRSof7v0QCLcBGAs/s1600/boxplot1.png\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-TjWTyYUesQs/WVRrSBYHI1I/AAAAAAAAACI/EXh9smfCdF4riP9vi2pbVGqcIRSof7v0QCLcBGAs/s1600/boxplot1.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366987688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tOkATfJggLHotDPV7ca3P\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-TjWTyYUesQs/WVRrSBYHI1I/AAAAAAAAACI/EXh9smfCdF4riP9vi2pbVGqcIRSof7v0QCLcBGAs/s320/boxplot1.png\" height=\"320\" width=\"320\" border=\"0\"></a></p>The second plot results in the appropriate spacing on the axis, but not the grouping. <br><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-z2a9pSCgbmo/WVRrqqe41NI/AAAAAAAAACM/SXA9IdwNiwgZLh7NPoSbP0Nre7PUq1MugCLcBGAs/s1600/boxplot2.png\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-z2a9pSCgbmo/WVRrqqe41NI/AAAAAAAAACM/SXA9IdwNiwgZLh7NPoSbP0Nre7PUq1MugCLcBGAs/s1600/boxplot2.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366987688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Dvj5ffG81vSA2nNSPzKZZ\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-z2a9pSCgbmo/WVRrqqe41NI/AAAAAAAAACM/SXA9IdwNiwgZLh7NPoSbP0Nre7PUq1MugCLcBGAs/s320/boxplot2.png\" height=\"320\" width=\"320\" border=\"0\"></a></p><br>Any suggestions on how to combe the two?<br><br>Many thanks in advance,<br>Emma<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br><br><br><br></font></span></div></span><span><font color=\"#888888\"><span>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366987688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2E3iOSnEJVoiVotsZJOnNZ\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br></span>\r\nTo post: email <a rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><span><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366987688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1n-he7xHaTvH1UmasfPay1\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n<br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggplot2&quot; group.<br></span>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<span><br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366987688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3IQQELIRpzb4hzBeWn7ggn\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</span></font></span></blockquote></div><br><br clear=\"all\"><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div><a href=\"http://hadley.nz\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://hadley.nz&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366987688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw02MlSK2JzlewX0LMfWcdxw\">http://hadley.nz</a></div>\r\n</font></span></div>\r\n</blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
